<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Technical lemmas</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we collect the technical lemmas required for our proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a convex and compact set that contains at least one interior point.
Then there exist constants <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{K},r_{K}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{K},r_{K}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;r\leq r_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;r\leq r_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vol\big(\mathcal{B}(x,r)\cap K\big)\geq\rho_{K}r^{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vol\big(\mathcal{B}(x,r)\cap K\big)\geq\rho_{K}r^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Projection is to close to a tilted mean)<span id="A1.Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a convex and compact set that contains at least one interior point.
For any <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\notin K</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{\sigma}(z)=\int_{K}x\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{\sigma}(z)=\int_{K}x\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalizing coefficient defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma}(z)=\int_{K}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma}(z)=\int_{K}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, there exists a constant <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{K}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{K}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,
such that for all <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}\left(m_{\sigma}(z),\Proj_{K}(z)\right)\leq C_{K}\,\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}\left(m_{\sigma}(z),\Proj_{K}(z)\right)\leq C_{K}\,\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Projection is to close to a tilted mean). ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Projection is to close to a tilted mean). ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We then define the Hausdorff distance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefn1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefn1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefn1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hausdorff distance)<span id="A1.Thmdefn1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefn1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmdefn1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefn1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmdefn1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be two compact sets.
Then, their Hausdorff distance, denoted by <math id="A1.Thmdefn1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(X,Y)=\max\left\{\sup_{x\in X}\mathsf{dist}(x,Y),\,\sup_{y\in Y}\mathsf{dist}(y,X)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(X,Y)=\max\left\{\sup_{x\in X}\mathsf{dist}(x,Y),\,\sup_{y\in Y}\mathsf{dist}(y,X)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmrem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmrem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmrem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmrem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmrem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Thmrem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> defines a metric on the space of non-empty compact subsets in <math id="A1.Thmrem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmrem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmrem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmrem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmrem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmrem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is well-known that convex sets can be approximated arbitrarily well by convex sets with algebraic (and hence smooth) surfaces <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Firey, 1974</a>)</cite>.
More precisely, for any <math id="A1.Thmrem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and any compact convex set <math id="A1.Thmrem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists another compact convex set <math id="A1.Thmrem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}</annotation></semantics></math> with smooth boundary, such that <math id="A1.Thmrem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(\widetilde{K},K)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d}_{\mathsf{H}}(\widetilde{K},K)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact, convex set with <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-boundary, where <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the function <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\mathsf{dist}(x,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\mathsf{dist}(x,K)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}\setminus K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}\setminus K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, the Laplacian of this function is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathsf{dist}(x,K)=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\frac{\kappa_{i}(\Proj_{K}(x))}{1+\kappa_{i}(\Proj_{K}(x))\mathsf{dist}(x,K)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathsf{dist}(x,K)=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\frac{\kappa_{i}(\Proj_{K}(x))}{1+\kappa_{i}(\Proj_{K}(x))\mathsf{dist}(x,K)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\kappa_{i}\right\}_{1\leq i\leq n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\kappa_{i}\right\}_{1\leq i\leq n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the principal curvatures of <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial K</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, since <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial K</annotation></semantics></math> is compact,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathsf{dist}(x,K)\leq\mathcal{C}_{K}=n\sup_{y\in\partial K}\max_{1\leq i\leq n-1}\kappa_{i}(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathsf{dist}(x,K)\leq\mathcal{C}_{K}=n\sup_{y\in\partial K}\max_{1\leq i\leq n-1}\kappa_{i}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> </h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lemma is trivial when <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>. In what follows, we consider <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be an interior point of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{K}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{K}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(v_{K},\delta_{K})\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(v_{K},\delta_{K})\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define a mapping <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{K}\colon\partial K\mapsto\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{K}\colon\partial K\mapsto\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{K}(x)=\inf_{0&lt;r&lt;r_{K}}\frac{\vol\big(\mathcal{B}(x,r)\cap K\big)}{r^{d}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{K}(x)=\inf_{0&lt;r&lt;r_{K}}\frac{\vol\big(\mathcal{B}(x,r)\cap K\big)}{r^{d}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{K}=\inf_{x\in\partial K}\left\|v_{K}-x\right\|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{K}=\inf_{x\in\partial K}\left\|v_{K}-x\right\|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
To prove the lemma, it suffices to show <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{x\in\partial K}F_{K}(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{x\in\partial K}F_{K}(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{\alpha x+(1-\alpha)z:z\in\mathcal{B}(v_{K},\delta_{K}),\,\alpha\in[0,1]\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{\alpha x+(1-\alpha)z:z\in\mathcal{B}(v_{K},\delta_{K}),\,\alpha\in[0,1]\big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\left\langle y-v_{K},x-v_{K}\right\rangle\geq 0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\left\langle y-v_{K},x-v_{K}\right\rangle\geq 0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{C}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{C}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{x}\cap H_{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{x}\cap H_{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By convexity, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{x}\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{x}\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that for all <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,r_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,r_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vol\big(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\big)\geq\vol\big(\widetilde{C}_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\big)\geq\left(\frac{r}{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|}\right)^{d}\cdot\vol\big(\widetilde{C}_{x}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vol\big(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\big)\geq\vol\big(\widetilde{C}_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\big)\geq\left(\frac{r}{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|}\right)^{d}\cdot\vol\big(\widetilde{C}_{x}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is a cone with base being a <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional ball that has radius <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vol\left(\widetilde{C}_{x}\right)=\frac{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\cdot\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vol\left(\widetilde{C}_{x}\right)=\frac{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\cdot\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the volume of a <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional ball.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vol\left(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vol\left(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\left(\frac{r}{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|}\right)^{d}\cdot\frac{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\cdot\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\left(\frac{r}{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|}\right)^{d}\cdot\frac{\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\cdot\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|^{d-1}}\cdot r^{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|^{d-1}}\cdot r^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\leq\mathsf{diam}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|x-v_{K}\right\|\leq\mathsf{diam}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that for all <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,r_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,r_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vol\left(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vol\left(C_{x}\cap\mathcal{B}(x,r)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\cdot\mathsf{diam}(K)^{d-1}}\cdot r^{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗆</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\cdot\mathsf{diam}(K)^{d-1}}\cdot r^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">The lemma follows by setting <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{K}=\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\cdot\mathsf{diam}(K)^{d-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗆</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{K}=\frac{\omega_{d-1}\cdot\delta_{K}^{d-1}}{d\cdot\mathsf{diam}(K)^{d-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Projection is to close to a tilted mean). ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\Proj_{K}(z)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\Proj_{K}(z)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\mathsf{dist}(z,K)=\left\|z-p\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\mathsf{dist}(z,K)=\left\|z-p\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
By convexity of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the hyperplane</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\left\langle x-p,\,\nu_{p}\right\rangle=0\right\},\qquad\nu_{p}=\frac{p-z}{\left\|p-z\right\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\left\langle x-p,\,\nu_{p}\right\rangle=0\right\},\qquad\nu_{p}=\frac{p-z}{\left\|p-z\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is a supporting hyperplane for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\left\{x:\left\langle x-p,\nu_{p}\right\rangle\geq 0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\left\{x:\left\langle x-p,\nu_{p}\right\rangle\geq 0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(x)=\left\langle x-p,\nu_{p}\right\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(x)=\left\langle x-p,\nu_{p}\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By the supporting hyperplane property, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then partition <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> according to its distance to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{1,r}=\{x\in K:d_{H}(x)\leq r\},\qquad K_{2,r}=\{x\in K:d_{H}(x)&gt;r\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{1,r}=\{x\in K:d_{H}(x)\leq r\},\qquad K_{2,r}=\{x\in K:d_{H}(x)&gt;r\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We can then upper bound <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-p\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-p\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> using the following two terms:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-p\right\|\leq\underbrace{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}}_{\mathrm{I}}+\underbrace{\int_{K_{2,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}}_{\mathrm{II}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>I</mi></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>II</mi></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-p\right\|\leq\underbrace{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}}_{\mathrm{I}}+\underbrace{\int_{K_{2,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}}_{\mathrm{II}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We then control terms <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{II}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>II</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{II}</annotation></semantics></math> separately below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Bounding term I</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For notational simplicity, define <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{\sigma}(x)=\exp(-\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}/(2\sigma^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\sigma}(x)=\exp(-\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}/(2\sigma^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can then upper bound term <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{I}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{I}=\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\,w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}\leq\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\,w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{I}=\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\,w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}\leq\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\,w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}x}=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1,r}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\mathds{1}_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1,r}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\mathds{1}_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math>.
We next prove that</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big]\leq r+\sqrt{d}\,\sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big]\leq r+\sqrt{d}\,\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, via translation and rotation,
we will assume that <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}=e_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}=e_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (the <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th standard basis in <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>).
In this case, for <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},x_{2},\cdots,x_{d})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},x_{2},\cdots,x_{d})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(x)=x_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(x)=x_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1,r}\subseteq\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\,x_{d}\in[0,r]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1,r}\subseteq\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\,x_{d}\in[0,r]\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[|X_{d}|\big]+\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq r+\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X-p\right\|\big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[|X_{d}|\big]+\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq r+\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We then upper bound <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(u)=\sup\{\theta\geq 0:\,\theta u\in K_{1,r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(u)=\sup\{\theta\geq 0:\,\theta u\in K_{1,r}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Rewriting this expectation in spherical coordinates, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\,\mathrm{d}u}{\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\,\mathrm{d}u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\,\mathrm{d}u}{\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\,\mathrm{d}u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+\alpha(u)\delta)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha(u)=\left\|u_{1:(d-1)}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(u)=\left\|u_{1:(d-1)}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and recall <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\mathsf{dist}(z,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\mathsf{dist}(z,H)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then upper bound the right-hand side of <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Bounding term I ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.
To this end, for <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{u}(w)=\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{u}(w)=\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{u,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{u,w}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable with density function <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{u,w}(r)\propto\mathds{1}_{r\in[0,\theta(u)]}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u,w}(r)\propto\mathds{1}_{r\in[0,\theta(u)]}r^{d-1}e^{-(r+w)^{2}/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}(w)=\mathbb{E}[R_{u,w}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}(w)=\mathbb{E}[R_{u,w}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking the derivative of <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{u}^{\prime}(w)=-\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\mathsf{Var}[R_{u,w}]\leq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{u}^{\prime}(w)=-\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\mathsf{Var}[R_{u,w}]\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}(w)\leq f_{u}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}(w)\leq f_{u}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this upper bound into <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Bounding term I ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq\sup_{u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq\sup_{u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\frac{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\theta(u)}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">We claim that the function</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto\frac{\int_{0}^{y}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto\frac{\int_{0}^{y}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">is increasing on <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, differentiating the function with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\left(y^{d}e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right)\cdot\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)-\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)\cdot\left(y^{d-1}e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right)}{\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\left(y^{d}e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right)\cdot\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)-\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)\cdot\left(y^{d-1}e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right)}{\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)^{2}}\cdot\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}(y-r)\,\mathrm{d}r\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{e^{-y^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{\left(\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r\right)^{2}}\cdot\int_{0}^{y}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}(y-r)\,\mathrm{d}r\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq\frac{\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}=\frac{\sqrt{2}\sigma\Gamma((d+1)/2)}{\Gamma(d/2)}\leq\sigma\sqrt{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mu_{1,r}}\big[\left\|X_{1:(d-1)}\right\|\big]\leq\frac{\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}{\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}e^{-r^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}r}=\frac{\sqrt{2}\sigma\Gamma((d+1)/2)}{\Gamma(d/2)}\leq\sigma\sqrt{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Gamma function.
Combining the above upper bound with <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Bounding term I ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Bounding term I ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> completes the proof of <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Bounding term I ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Bounding term II</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{II}=\int_{K_{2,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}\leq\frac{\mbox{diam}(K)}{1+\underbrace{\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K_{2,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}_{{}_{\diamondsuit}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>II</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>diam</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♢</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{II}=\int_{K_{2,r}}\left\|x-p\right\|\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\frac{\,\mathrm{d}x}{p_{\sigma}(z)}\leq\frac{\mbox{diam}(K)}{1+\underbrace{\frac{\int_{K_{1,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\mathrm{d}x}{\int_{K_{2,r}}w_{\sigma}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}_{{}_{\diamondsuit}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mbox{diam}(K)=\sup\{\|x-y\|:\,x,y\in K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>diam</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{diam}(K)=\sup\{\|x-y\|:\,x,y\in K\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then lower bound term <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\diamondsuit}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\diamondsuit}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observe that <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)\subseteq K_{1,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)\subseteq K_{1,r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|x-z\right\|\leq\left\|x-p\right\|+\left\|z-p\right\|\leq\frac{r}{2}+\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|x-z\right\|\leq\left\|x-p\right\|+\left\|z-p\right\|\leq\frac{r}{2}+\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{K_{1,r}}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x&amp;\geq\int_{K_{1,r/2}\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\vol\left(K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)\right)\cdot\exp\Big(-\frac{(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\\
&amp;\geq\rho_{K}\left(\frac{r}{2}\right)^{d}\exp\Big(-\frac{(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{K_{1,r}}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x&amp;\geq\int_{K_{1,r/2}\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\vol\left(K\cap\mathcal{B}(p,r/2)\right)\cdot\exp\Big(-\frac{(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\\
&amp;\geq\rho_{K}\left(\frac{r}{2}\right)^{d}\exp\Big(-\frac{(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
On the other hand, <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(z)=-\left\|z-p\right\|=-\delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(z)=-\left\|z-p\right\|=-\delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> fall on different sides of <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, and the segment connecting them intersects <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> at a point <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using this, we see that for <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{2,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{2,r}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|x-z\right\|=\left\|x-h\right\|+\left\|z-h\right\|\geq d_{H}(x)+\left\|z-p\right\|\geq r+\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|x-z\right\|=\left\|x-h\right\|+\left\|z-h\right\|\geq d_{H}(x)+\left\|z-p\right\|\geq r+\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which further implies that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{K_{2,r}}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x\leq\vol(K)\exp\Big(-\frac{(r+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{K_{2,r}}\exp\Big(-\frac{\left\|x-z\right\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)\,\mathrm{d}x\leq\vol(K)\exp\Big(-\frac{(r+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Combining <a href="#A1.E25" title="In Bounding term II ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E26" title="Equation 26 ‣ Bounding term II ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>, we obtain the following lower bound for <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamondsuit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamondsuit</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\diamondsuit&amp;\geq\frac{\rho_{K}(r/2)^{d}}{\vol(K)}\exp\Big(\,\frac{(r+\delta)^{2}-(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\,\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{\rho_{K}}{2^{d}\vol(K)}\cdot r^{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{3r^{2}/4+r\delta}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi mathvariant="normal">♢</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.340em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\diamondsuit&amp;\geq\frac{\rho_{K}(r/2)^{d}}{\vol(K)}\exp\Big(\,\frac{(r+\delta)^{2}-(r/2+\delta)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\,\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{\rho_{K}}{2^{d}\vol(K)}\cdot r^{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{3r^{2}/4+r\delta}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Proof of the lemma</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We then separately discuss two cases depending on the value of <math id="A1.SS2.SSSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, then we let <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging this choice and <a href="#A1.E27" title="In Bounding term II ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> into <a href="#A1.E24" title="In Bounding term II ‣ A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, and combining this with the upper bound from Step I, we obtain that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-\Proj_{K}(z)\right\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-\Proj_{K}(z)\right\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{1}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{r\delta+3r^{2}/4}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{1}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{r\delta+3r^{2}/4}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{1}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{r\delta}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,(2d+2)\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{1}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{r\delta}{2\sigma^{2}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{2}\,\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{2}\,\sigma\log\sigma^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive constants that depend only on <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta\leq\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta\leq\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=2\sqrt{d+1}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\sigma^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=2\sqrt{d+1}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\sigma^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-\Proj_{K}(z)\right\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|m_{\sigma}(z)-\Proj_{K}(z)\right\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\sqrt{d+1}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\sigma^{-1}}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{3}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{3r^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\sqrt{d+1}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\sigma^{-1}}+\sqrt{d}\sigma+C_{3}r^{-d}\exp\Big(-\frac{3r^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{3}\sigma\log\sigma^{-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{3}\sigma\log\sigma^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3},C_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3},C_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive constants that depend only on <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is done.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proof is adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gilbarg and Trudinger, 1977</a>, Theorem 14.16)</cite>.
For notational convenience, we write <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{K}(x)=\mathsf{dist}(x,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{K}(x)=\mathsf{dist}(x,K)</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the inward-pointing unit normal vector field on <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial K</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\partial K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\partial K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla d_{K}(x)=-\nu_{\partial K}(\Proj_{K}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla d_{K}(x)=-\nu_{\partial K}(\Proj_{K}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K</annotation></semantics></math>,
it suffices to show <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla d_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla d_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, for each point <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\not\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\not\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\Proj_{K}(x)\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\Proj_{K}(x)\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|y-x\right\|=d_{K}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|y-x\right\|=d_{K}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, the points <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the following equation</p>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y-\nu_{\partial K}(y)d_{K}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y-\nu_{\partial K}(y)d_{K}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For a fixed point <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K</annotation></semantics></math>,
let <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=\Proj_{K}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=\Proj_{K}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose a principal coordinate system at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\partial K}(y_{0})=e_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\partial K}(y_{0})=e_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=0_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=0_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> under this coordinate system, and the principal curvatures at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{1},\dots,\kappa_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{1},\dots,\kappa_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will work in this principal coordinate system throughout the remainder of the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define a mapping <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(g_{1},\dots,g_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(g_{1},\dots,g_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\Pi(\mathcal{N}(y_{0})\cap T(y_{0}))\times\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\Pi(\mathcal{N}(y_{0})\cap T(y_{0}))\times\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\colon(y^{\prime},t)\mapsto\Phi(y^{\prime})+t\cdot\nu_{\partial K}\circ\Phi(y^{\prime}),\quad\Phi(y^{\prime})=(y^{\prime},\phi(y^{\prime}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\colon(y^{\prime},t)\mapsto\Phi(y^{\prime})+t\cdot\nu_{\partial K}\circ\Phi(y^{\prime}),\quad\Phi(y^{\prime})=(y^{\prime},\phi(y^{\prime})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(y_{0})=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\langle x,e_{n}\rangle=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(y_{0})=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\langle x,e_{n}\rangle=0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the tangent space at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is a neighborhood of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial K\cap\mathcal{N}(y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial K\cap\mathcal{N}(y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented as the graph of a <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> convex function <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\colon\Pi(T(y_{0})\cap\mathcal{N}(y_{0}))\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\colon\Pi(T(y_{0})\cap\mathcal{N}(y_{0}))\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the projection onto the first <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\partial K}\in C^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\partial K}\in C^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in C^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in C^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in C^{k-1}(\mathcal{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in C^{k-1}(\mathcal{U})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}\in\Pi(\mathcal{N}(y_{0})\cap T(y_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}\in\Pi(\mathcal{N}(y_{0})\cap T(y_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin K</annotation></semantics></math>, the total derivative matrix of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\prime},-d_{K}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\prime},-d_{K}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> (with respect to the principal coordinate system) is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla g(y^{\prime},-d_{K}(x))=\mathrm{diag}\begin{pmatrix}1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{1},\,1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{2},\,\dots,\,1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{n-1},\,1\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla g(y^{\prime},-d_{K}(x))=\mathrm{diag}\begin{pmatrix}1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{1},\,1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{2},\,\dots,\,1+d_{K}(x)\kappa_{n-1},\,1\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gilbarg and Trudinger, 1977</a>, Section 14.16)</cite> for more details.
Then the Jacobian of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\left(\nabla g(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(1+d_{K}(x_{0})\kappa_{i})\neq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\left(\nabla g(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(1+d_{K}(x_{0})\kappa_{i})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))=x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(0_{d-1},-d_{K}(x_{0}))=x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the inverse mapping theorem implies that for some neighborhood <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mapping <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-diffeomorphism between <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the mapping</p>
<table id="A1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Proj_{K}(x)=\big(\,\Pi\circ g^{-1}(x),\,\phi(\Pi\circ g^{-1}(x))\,\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Proj_{K}(x)=\big(\,\Pi\circ g^{-1}(x),\,\phi(\Pi\circ g^{-1}(x))\,\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">is <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla d_{K}(x)=-\nu_{\partial K}\circ\Proj_{K}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla d_{K}(x)=-\nu_{\partial K}\circ\Proj_{K}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we see that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla d_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla d_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{K}\in C^{k}(\mathcal{A}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{K}\in C^{k}(\mathcal{A}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary, we conclude that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{K}\in C^{k}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{K}\in C^{k}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we compute <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta d_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta d_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We claim that the Hessian matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}d_{K}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}d_{K}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the principal coordinate system at <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}d_{K}(x_{0})=\mathrm{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\frac{\kappa_{1}}{1+\kappa_{1}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,\frac{\kappa_{2}}{1+\kappa_{2}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,\dots,\,\frac{\kappa_{n-1}}{1+\kappa_{n-1}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,0\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}d_{K}(x_{0})=\mathrm{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\frac{\kappa_{1}}{1+\kappa_{1}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,\frac{\kappa_{2}}{1+\kappa_{2}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,\dots,\,\frac{\kappa_{n-1}}{1+\kappa_{n-1}d_{K}(x_{0})},\,0\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[n-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[n-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, inverting the matrix given in <a href="#A1.E28" title="In A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{ij}d_{K}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{ij}d_{K}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\partial_{i}\left(\nu^{j}_{\partial K}\circ g^{-1}(x_{0})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\partial_{i}\left(\nu^{j}_{\partial K}\circ g^{-1}(x_{0})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\langle\nabla\nu_{\partial K}^{j}(y_{0}),\partial_{i}g^{-1}(x_{0})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\langle\nabla\nu_{\partial K}^{j}(y_{0}),\partial_{i}g^{-1}(x_{0})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa_{i}}{1+\kappa_{i}d_{K}(x_{0})}\cdot\mathds{1}_{i=j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa_{i}}{1+\kappa_{i}d_{K}(x_{0})}\cdot\mathds{1}_{i=j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, for any <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{n,i}d_{K}(x_{0})=-\partial_{n}\left(\nu^{i}_{\partial K}\circ g^{-1}(x_{0})\right)=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{n,i}d_{K}(x_{0})=-\partial_{n}\left(\nu^{i}_{\partial K}\circ g^{-1}(x_{0})\right)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\partial K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\partial K}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant in the <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{n}=\nu_{\partial K}(y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{n}=\nu_{\partial K}(y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> direction.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta d_{K}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta d_{K}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\frac{\kappa_{i}}{1+\kappa_{i}d_{K}(x_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\frac{\kappa_{i}}{1+\kappa_{i}d_{K}(x_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">as desired.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs for guided DDIM</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the theorem, we first establish the following lemma, which controls the derivative of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> close to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> that depends solely on <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&gt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&gt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[\tau_{\varepsilon},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[\tau_{\varepsilon},T)</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the theorem, it suffices to show for any fixed <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{t\to T}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{t\to T}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> be the time lower bound in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.
First, we show that there exists <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})&gt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})&gt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, applying Grönwall’s inequality and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>,
we see that for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau_{\varepsilon}},K_{\eta_{0}})\exp\left(-\int_{\tau_{\varepsilon}}^{\tau}\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-\tau}^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}\tau\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau_{\varepsilon}},K_{\eta_{0}})\exp\left(-\int_{\tau_{\varepsilon}}^{\tau}\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-\tau}^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}\tau\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">implying that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau},K_{\eta_{0}})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau},K_{\eta_{0}})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to T</annotation></semantics></math>.
A contradiction.
Therefore, there exists <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;\tau^{\prime}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{\tau^{\prime}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now, since the map <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing whenever <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;t&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;t&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>,
we see that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\prime}\leq t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\prime}\leq t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>.
The proof is completed by mapping the problem back to the <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-space and noting that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{x}_{t})_{0\leq t&lt;T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{x}_{t})_{0\leq t&lt;T}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
Define <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t}=\lambda_{T-t_{k}}^{-1}\widehat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t}=\lambda_{T-t_{k}}^{-1}\widehat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, then on the same interval,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\widehat{z}_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\widehat{z}_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\widehat{z}_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t+\left\{\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left(m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left(m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)\right\}\mathrm{d}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\widehat{z}_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t+\left\{\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left(m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left(m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)\right\}\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The above equation implies that for all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\\
&amp;=(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\Big(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left(m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left(m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)\Big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\\
&amp;=(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\Big(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left(m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left(m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right)\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">To prove the theorem, we first establish the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=\inf_{y\in K_{\eta},\,y^{\prime}\in K_{\eta^{\prime}},\,\eta\neq\eta^{\prime}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=\inf_{y\in K_{\eta},\,y^{\prime}\in K_{\eta^{\prime}},\,\eta\neq\eta^{\prime}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, with a sufficiently small <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\tau_{0}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\tau_{0}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> that also depends only on <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq d_{0}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq d_{0}/3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}\in[\tau_{0},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}\in[\tau_{0},T)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\leq-\frac{2}{5\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\leq-\frac{2}{5\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> implies that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> will eventually enter a region closer to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> than to any other component. We then show that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> subsequently approaches <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>,
with a sufficiently small <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>,
for any <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\min\{1,d_{0}/3\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\min\{1,d_{0}/3\})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\tau_{\varepsilon}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> that depends solely on <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},\varepsilon,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},\varepsilon,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}\in[\tau_{\varepsilon},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}\in[\tau_{\varepsilon},T)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\leq-\frac{2}{5\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\leq-\frac{2}{5\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, with a sufficiently small <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\delta},\overline{\tau}_{\delta}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\delta},\overline{\tau}_{\delta}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depend only on <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta,p_{0},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta,p_{0},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> that satisfies </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}\in[\overline{\tau}_{\delta},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}\in[\overline{\tau}_{\delta},T)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for all </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> we have </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\delta}&lt;d_{0}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\delta}&lt;d_{0}/3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. In addition, </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\delta}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\delta}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS6" title="B.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove the theorem using the above lemmas.
Choose <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small so that the conditions of Lemmas <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>–<a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> are satisfied.
For any <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
define <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\tau}_{\delta}=\max\{\tau_{0},\tau_{\varepsilon_{\delta}},\overline{\tau}_{\delta}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\tau}_{\delta}=\max\{\tau_{0},\tau_{\varepsilon_{\delta}},\overline{\tau}_{\delta}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\delta}\in\mathbb{N}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\delta}\in\mathbb{N}+</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{k_{\delta}}&gt;\widetilde{\tau}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k_{\delta}}&gt;\widetilde{\tau}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, there exists <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\geq k_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\geq k_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k^{\prime}}},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;\varepsilon_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k^{\prime}}},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;\varepsilon_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we conclude that for any <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq k^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq k^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k^{\prime}}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon_{\delta}+\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k^{\prime}}},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\varepsilon_{\delta}+\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">The statememt of the theorem then follows by letting <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the set <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, the distance function <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(\cdot,K_{\eta_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(\cdot,K_{\eta_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K_{\eta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus K_{\eta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Federer, 1959</a>, Theorem 4.8 Part(5))</cite>.
Therefore, by the chain rule and the ODE reformulation (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ 3.2 Intuition: reformulating DDIM with guidance ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})=\left\langle\frac{z_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})}{\left\|z_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})\right\|},\,\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}{z}_{t}\right\rangle\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\langle\frac{z_{t}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})}{\left\|z_{t}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})\right\|},\,\gamma F_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})-(\gamma-1)\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})F_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\rangle,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})=\left\langle\frac{z_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})}{\left\|z_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})\right\|},\,\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}{z}_{t}\right\rangle\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\langle\frac{z_{t}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})}{\left\|z_{t}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t})\right\|},\,\gamma F_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})-(\gamma-1)\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})F_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\rangle,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we recall that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\eta,T-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\eta,T-t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.2 Intuition: reformulating DDIM with guidance ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
For <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\eta,t}(z)=\Proj_{K_{\eta}}(z)-m_{\eta,t}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\eta,t}(z)=\Proj_{K_{\eta}}(z)-m_{\eta,t}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as the difference between the projection <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Proj_{K_{\eta}}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Proj_{K_{\eta}}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and the tilted mean <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\eta,t}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\eta,t}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.2 Intuition: reformulating DDIM with guidance ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we see that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\text{Equation~\eqref{eqn:dist_deriv}}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\gamma-(\gamma-1)\zeta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\cdot\Big[-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big]\\
&amp;\qquad+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\cdot\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})+\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big]\\
&amp;=\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\cdot\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big(\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Equation (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‖</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\text{Equation~\eqref{eqn:dist_deriv}}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\gamma-(\gamma-1)\zeta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\cdot\Big[-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big]\\
&amp;\qquad+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\cdot\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})+\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big]\\
&amp;=\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\cdot\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big(\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\neq\eta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\neq\eta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze <a href="#A2.E32" title="In B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> by dividing the index set <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> into three subsets.
Specifically, for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the following three time-dependent sets:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq 2\cdot\Xi_{T-t}\right\},\\
\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:0\leq\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;2\cdot\Xi_{T-t}\right\},\\
\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&lt;}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;0\right\},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq 2\cdot\Xi_{T-t}\right\},\\
\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:0\leq\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;2\cdot\Xi_{T-t}\right\},\\
\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&lt;}&amp;=\left\{\eta\in\mathcal{I}:\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})&lt;0\right\},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi_{T-t}=\sqrt{\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi_{T-t}=\sqrt{\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}=\lambda_{T-t}^{-2}\sigma_{T-t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}=\lambda_{T-t}^{-2}\sigma_{T-t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that the above three sets do not overlap, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}\sqcup\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}\sqcup\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&lt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup><mo>⊔</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup><mo>⊔</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}\sqcup\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}\sqcup\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&lt;}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the above notations, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mbox{The last line of Equation \eqref{eqn:dist_derive_II}}\\
&amp;\leq\underbrace{\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}_{\rm I}\\
&amp;\quad+\underbrace{\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}_{\rm II}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big(\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>The last line of Equation (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>I</mi></munder></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>II</mi></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mbox{The last line of Equation \eqref{eqn:dist_derive_II}}\\
&amp;\leq\underbrace{\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}_{\rm I}\\
&amp;\quad+\underbrace{\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}_{\rm II}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\neq\eta_{0}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big(\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|+\left\|\Delta_{\eta_{0},T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">To bound term <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rm I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rm I</annotation></semantics></math>, observe that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})=\inf_{y\in K_{\eta}}\left\|z_{t}-y\right\|-\inf_{y\in K_{0}}\left\|z_{t}-y\right\|\leq\sup_{y\in K_{\eta},y^{\prime}\in K_{\eta_{0}}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|\leq D_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})=\inf_{y\in K_{\eta}}\left\|z_{t}-y\right\|-\inf_{y\in K_{0}}\left\|z_{t}-y\right\|\leq\sup_{y\in K_{\eta},y^{\prime}\in K_{\eta_{0}}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|\leq D_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{0}=\sup_{y,y^{\prime}\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{0}=\sup_{y,y^{\prime}\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We then upper bound <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})=\,\frac{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}w_{\eta}\int p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}\\
&amp;\leq\,\Bigg({1+\frac{w_{\eta_{0}}\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}}\Bigg)^{-1}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.618em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.618em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})=\,\frac{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}w_{\eta}\int p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}\\
&amp;\leq\,\Bigg({1+\frac{w_{\eta_{0}}\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}}\Bigg)^{-1}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">By the second point of Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmass1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we know that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{w_{\eta_{0}}\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}\geq w_{\eta_{0}}\cdot\frac{\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{w_{\eta_{0}}\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}w_{\eta}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}\geq w_{\eta_{0}}\cdot\frac{\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we know that there exists a constant <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{{\eta_{0}}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{{\eta_{0}}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}\cap\,\mathcal{B}(\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t}),\,\Xi_{T-t})}e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\vol\Big(K_{\eta_{0}}\cap\,\mathcal{B}\big(\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t}),\,\Xi_{T-t}\big)\Big)\cdot e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\\
&amp;\geq\,\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\,\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\cdot e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.392em">∩</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝗏𝗈𝗅</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.562em">∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.340em">≥</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}\cap\,\mathcal{B}(\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t}),\,\Xi_{T-t})}e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\,\mathrm{d}x\\
&amp;\geq\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\vol\Big(K_{\eta_{0}}\cap\,\mathcal{B}\big(\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(z_{t}),\,\Xi_{T-t}\big)\Big)\cdot e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\\
&amp;\geq\,\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\,\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\cdot e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, for all <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x\leq e^{-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\leq e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x\leq e^{-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\leq e^{-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.11" class="ltx_p">Combining <a href="#A2.E37" title="In B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, we conclude that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}\\
&amp;\geq\frac{\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}\cdot\exp\Big(\frac{(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\Big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\int_{K_{\eta_{0}}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\,\mathrm{d}x}{\sum\limits_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\int_{K_{\eta}}p_{\eta}(x)\,e^{-\left\|x-z_{t}\right\|^{2}/(2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2})}\mathrm{d}x}\\
&amp;\geq\frac{\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}\cdot\exp\Big(\frac{(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Putting together <a href="#A2.E35" title="In B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, <a href="#A2.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>,
we see that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}\cdot\exp\Big(-\frac{(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\Big)\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}\cdot\exp\Big(-\frac{(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+2\Xi_{T-t})^{2}-(\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\Xi_{T-t})^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\Big)\\
&amp;\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.13" class="ltx_p">In summary, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-t}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}{\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{&gt;}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-t}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.14" class="ltx_p">which upper bounds term <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rm I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rm I</annotation></semantics></math>.
To bound term <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rm II" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>II</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rm II</annotation></semantics></math>, simply observe that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]\leq\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-t}}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≈</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}_{t}^{\approx}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\Big[\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta})-\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\Big]\leq\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-t}}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.15" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Projection is to close to a tilted mean). ‣ Appendix A Technical lemmas ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we know that</p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\leq C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-t}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-t}^{-2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\Delta_{\eta,T-t}(z_{t})\right\|\leq C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-t}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-t}^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.16" class="ltx_p">for some positive constant <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{K_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{K_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, combining the upper bounds in <a href="#A2.E34" title="In B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>, <a href="#A2.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>, <a href="#A2.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>,
we see that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-t}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-t}}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-t}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-t}^{-2})}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-t}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-t}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-t}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-t}}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-t}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-t}^{-2})}{\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.17" class="ltx_p">We then can choose <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently close to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for all <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\geq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}})\leq-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{T-t}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(z_{t},K_{\eta_{0}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.18" class="ltx_p">The proof is done.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{k},t_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, differentiating <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|=\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\widehat{z}_{t}\right\rangle\\
&amp;=\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\widehat{z}_{t}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle\\
&amp;=e^{t-t_{k}}\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|=\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\widehat{z}_{t}\right\rangle\\
&amp;=\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\widehat{z}_{t}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle\\
&amp;=e^{t-t_{k}}\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the second to last equality is by <a href="#A2.E29" title="In B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, and the last equality is by <a href="#A2.E30" title="In B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>.
Decomposing <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math> as the sum of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|=\frac{e^{t-t_{k}}}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|}\cdot\big(\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)+\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|=\frac{e^{t-t_{k}}}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|}\cdot\big(\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)+\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)=\left\langle\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle,\\
&amp;\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)=\left\langle\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}),\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)=\left\langle\widehat{z}_{t}-\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle,\\
&amp;\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)=\left\langle\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}),\,\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{0}=\sup_{y,y^{\prime}\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}=\sup_{y,y^{\prime}\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y-y^{\prime}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{0}=\sup_{y\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}=\sup_{y\in\cup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}K_{\eta}}\left\|y\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#A2.E30" title="In B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>, we know that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)=&amp;(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\cdot\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\,(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\cdot\Big(\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left\|m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left\|\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|\Big)^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\,(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\Big(\frac{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}+1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+R_{0}+\frac{\gamma D_{0}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\Big)^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\frac{3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)(\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}+1)^{2}\,\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{4}}+3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)R_{0}^{2}+\frac{3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\gamma^{2}D_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{4}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗃</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathsf{F}_{1}(t)=&amp;(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\cdot\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}+\frac{\gamma}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}F_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\,(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\cdot\Big(\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}\right\|+\frac{\gamma-1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\left\|m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-m_{\eta,T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left\|\Proj_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-m_{\eta_{0},T-t_{k}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|\Big)^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\,(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\Big(\frac{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}+1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+R_{0}+\frac{\gamma D_{0}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\Big)^{2}\\
\leq&amp;\frac{3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)(\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}+1)^{2}\,\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{4}}+3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)R_{0}^{2}+\frac{3(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\gamma^{2}D_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{4}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">By Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmass2" title="Assumption 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Summary of main results ‣ 3 Results for DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we see that for all <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t-t_{k}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t-t_{k}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{-2}(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\lesssim\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{-2}(e^{t-t_{k}}-1)\lesssim\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, where “<math id="A2.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lesssim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≲</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim</annotation></semantics></math>” hides a positive numerical constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As for <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, its upper bound is similar to the proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Specifically, by the upper bound in <a href="#A2.E44" title="In B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs for guided DDIM ‣ On the Robustness of Distribution Support under Diffusion Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>, we have (recall <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi_{T-t}=\sqrt{\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi_{T-t}=\sqrt{\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}=\lambda_{T-t}^{-2}\sigma_{T-t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-t}^{2}=\lambda_{T-t}^{-2}\sigma_{T-t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\gamma F_{\eta_{0},T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-(\gamma-1)\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle\\
&amp;\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-{t_{k}}}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\qquad+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{-2})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-t_{k}}^{2}}\left\langle\frac{\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})}{\left\|\widehat{z}_{t_{k}}-\mathrm{Proj}_{K_{\eta_{0}}}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\|},\,\gamma F_{\eta_{0},T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})-(\gamma-1)\sum_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}\zeta_{\eta,T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})F_{\eta,T-t}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}})\right\rangle\\
&amp;\leq\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-{t_{k}}}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\\
&amp;\qquad+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{-2})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The above upper bound implies the following bound for <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)\leq&amp;\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-{t_{k}}}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{-2})\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad+\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\big(\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+R_{0}\big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖽𝗂𝗌𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathsf{F}_{2}(t)\leq&amp;\frac{D_{0}(\gamma-1)\left|\mathcal{I}\right|\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{w_{\eta_{0}}\inf_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{\eta_{0}}(x)\cdot\rho_{\eta_{0}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{d}\sigma^{2}_{T-{t_{k}}}}\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{3\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}{2\widetilde{\sigma}_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(\gamma-1)\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})^{2}+\frac{2\gamma\sup_{\eta\in\mathcal{I}}C_{K_{\eta}}\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}\log(\Xi_{T-{t_{k}}}^{-2})\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})}{\sigma_{T-{t_{k}}}^{2}}\\
&amp;\qquad+\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})\big(\mathsf{dist}(\widehat{z}_{t_{k}},K_{\eta_{0}})+R_{0}\big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
